    "lawCode": "Amd §4-104, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6449\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to authorizing consol-\nidation of certain voting districts with a small number of eligible\nvoters\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo ensure the most efficient administration of election districts with\nvery few voters assigned.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill amends subdivision 5 paragraph a of § 4-104 of\nthe election law to provide that if an election district contains fewer\nthan ten voters eligible to vote in such election then the normal limi-\ntation of 500 maximum voters in a combined district shall not be appli-\ncable.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAs a result of the 2012 and 2013 redistricting of Congressional, State\nLegislative and city Council Districts, the Board of Elections in the\nCity of New York was mandated to draw approximately 250 newly created\nelection districts with 'zero eligible voters'. Many of these EDs\nconsist of empty tracts in the waters around the city, and likely never\nwill encompass registered voters. Part of the problem stems from the\ninconsistency between the boundaries drawn for the Congressional, State,\nand City Council districts and the boundaries established more than a\nhalf century ago for municipal Court Districts which elect some of the\nJudges of the Civil Court of New York.\n\nFurthermore, some EDs contain fewer than ten eligible voters. However,\nthe election law as currently written requires these EDs to be assigned\nto a poll site and boards of election may be unable to combine these EDs\nwith other EDs in those poll sites if the resulting election district\nhas more than 500 eligible voters. This requires significant expendi-\ntures of public funds, both in terms of personnel and equipment to staff\nand supply ED tables with few or zero voters. Therefore, enactment of\nthis bill is essential to provide boards of election with greater flexi-\nbility to combine EDs and reduce costs to tax payers.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nA.11120 of 2017-18.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nReduced election administrative costs for Board of Election.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
